task: scan-fold-without-tokens
agent: opus-optics
started: 2026-09-10
branch: feature/scan-fold
worktree: ../okay-wt-scanfold

why: the operator said "aggregation and scanners", the two doors
  opened today with no caller. One of them has a real one and the
  other does not, and this claim says which.

  REAL: `Provider.counting` and `Handlers.counter` count a message's
  BPE tokens as `Scan.all(bpe)(s).tokens.count(...)` — a Vector of
  every Token, each with a lexeme String and a Span, materialised to
  produce one Int, on every message. The sink road built this morning
  is exactly what removes it and has had no consumer outside the
  drivers.

  NOT REAL: the kaleidoscope and the classifying lens. okay-intent's
  nearest-centroid classifier IS aggregate-then-classify in shape, and
  rewriting it on the optics would be churn: the pooling is a tuned
  mutable loop the optic does not replace, and the code groups by slot
  before aggregating, so the composite buys nothing. Said in the
  entry rather than pretended.

what: `Scan.fold(sc)(input)(z)(f)` on `stepInto`, nothing
  materialised; `Scan.aggregate(sc)(input)(agg)` as the same with an
  `Aggregator`, which is the aggregation door that DOES fit here; and
  `Mealy.fold`, without which a composed machine still materialises.

measure: a bpeCount pair, folded against materialised, -prof gc.
  Allocation is the number.
